Implement Upgrade-31 as a bounded production-fleet safety slice for cvsz/zcoder.

Objective: add monotonic PostgreSQL fencing so stale continuous-engineering runners cannot persist upgrade ledger state after ownership moves to a newer runner.

Requirements:
- reuse the existing engineering_tasks table and zcoder_upgrade_ledger control metadata envelope;
- acquire a monotonically increasing fence_generation under SELECT ... FOR UPDATE;
- return a typed token carrying namespace, control row identity, and generation;
- validate the exact generation under the same row lock and transaction as each fenced task upsert;
- reject stale, missing, malformed, wrong-namespace, or invalid-generation tokens fail closed;
- preserve fence_generation when checkpoint/control metadata is written;
- add live DATABASE_URL integration coverage proving a stale generation cannot persist a task after a newer generation exists;
- keep PostgreSQL backend/CLI exposure disabled until Upgrade-28 ledger, Upgrade-30 advisory lease, and Upgrade-31 fencing are composed end to end;
- preserve Upgrade-20 execution authority, Upgrade-24 budgets, JSON/SQLite behavior, local-only push default, and all existing CI/security gates.
